# Prelude — system capabilities.
#
# Phantom capability atoms — declared here so atoms can `use` them.
# No runtime state, no methods; presence in a `use:` slot is a
# compile-time contract about what the enclosing atom is licensed
# to do.

# `use panic: SystemPanic` licenses the enclosing atom's body to call
# `panic("...")`. Without the declaration, `panic()` is a compile-
# time error pointing at this migration. Panic itself remains
# uncatchable per F31/F35 L2 — this is a compile-time gate, not a
# runtime dispatch.
def SystemPanic:
    -> ready

# `Uncaught(msg: String)` — reason record for exceptions that reach
# the atom-crash catch (F48 BEAM crash model) via any path that isn't
# a typed `|: as T(...)` proposition:
#   - Bare `|: cond` violations (no `as T`) — the invariant fired
#     but the user didn't declare a reason type.
#   - Cocoa exceptions bubbling up from `then:`/`do:` bodies
#     (NSRangeException, NSInvalidArgumentException, …).
#
# The L12c catch synthesizes an Uncaught box on non-typed catches so
# receiver-side `<:` dispatch on the reason sees a uniform, always-
# present object (no nil arm scrutinees). Companion-reason
# exhaustiveness (Track A/2.c) treats `:invariant-violation` entries
# in the reason universe as Uncaught arms.
def Uncaught:
    msg: String
